Standardy a sady
****************

{{description: Co přesně rozhodují vestavěné presety DressCode: standardy PER Coding Style 3.1, PSR-12, Nette a Symfony a sady modernizations, deprecations, cleanup, correctness, types a optimizedCalls, každý celým svým souborem.}}

.[perex]
Vestavěný preset je soubor téhož tvaru jako vaše konfigurace, takže nejlepší popis toho, co rozhoduje, je on sám. Tady je každý celý, i s komentáři, které říkají, proč má rozhodnutí svou hodnotu. Standardy rozhodují o vzhledu kódu a projekt si jeden vezme za základ, sady přidávají jeden záměr a dají se položit vedle kteréhokoli standardu.

Preset vychází z presetů, které jmenuje jeho klíč `use`, a mění jen to, co sám napíše; `nette` tedy stojí na `perCs` a ten na `psr12`. Co z toho všeho nakonec platí i s tím, odkud se každá hodnota vzala, vypíše `dresscode config --preset nette`. Jak se presety skládají s vaší konfigurací, popisuje stránka [Konfigurace |configuration#Standardy a sady], co znamená každý klíč, [Struktura konfigurace |decisions/@home].


Standardy
=========

Čtyři standardy rozhodují o všem, co vidíte: o odsazení, závorkách, mezerách, prázdných řádcích i zalamování. `psr12` a `perCs` jsou psané podle textu specifikací, oddíl po oddílu, a nic vlastního nepřidávají. `nette` a `symfony` stojí na PER Coding Style a přidávají, co chtějí jejich projekty.


`psr12`
=======

[PSR-12 |https://www.php-fig.org/psr/psr-12/], oddíl po oddílu.

```neon .[preset]
# PSR-12 Extended Coding Style
#
# PSR-12, section by section; the specification defines the style and this preset adds nothing of its own.

file:
	# the invisible bytes some editors put before `<?php`, which PHP would send as output
	bom: forbidden
	# `<?` and `<?PHP` are written `<?php`
	openingTag: '<?php'
	# a file of PHP alone ends without `?>`; a `?>` followed by HTML stays
	closingTagAtEnd: forbidden
	# every line ends as most lines of the file do, LF on a tie
	lineEnding: majority
	# the last line ends with a line ending, and no blank line follows it
	finalNewlines: 1
	# at the end of a line of code or of a comment; the text of a string stays as it is
	trailingWhitespace: forbidden
	# a signature or a condition wider than this is spread over lines; a line nothing can spread stays as it is
	maxLineLength: 120
	# `foo(); bar();` takes two lines, the header of a `for` counting as one statement
	statementsPerLine: 1
	# the second `;` of `foo();;` is removed rather than given a line of its own
	emptyStatements: forbidden

indentation:
	unit: '4 spaces'
	# a line opened by `&&`, `+` or `.` stands level with the start of its expression, `&& $b` right below `$a` in
	# a condition spread over lines, and one level deeper where the expression begins on the line of `$x =` or `return`
	binaryOperator: 0
	# `?` and `:` opening a line stand one level deeper than the line the ternary begins on
	ternary: 1
	# `case` one level inside `switch`, its statements one more
	switchCase: 1
	# every link of a chain spread over lines one level below the line the chain begins on:
	#     $query
	#         ->where($a)
	#         ->orderBy($b);
	chain: single

naming:
	# the case of names PSR-1 prescribes; a name in another case is reported and never renamed, the code using it
	# being anywhere, and a method of PHP such as `__construct()` passes
	class: PascalCase
	method: camelCase
	constant: UPPER_CASE

builtin:
	# `IF`, `Function`, `SELF` are written in lowercase
	keywords: lowercase
	# `TRUE`, `False`, `NULL` are written in lowercase
	trueFalseNull: lowercase
	# `Int`, `STRING`, `Void` in a declaration are written in lowercase
	types: lowercase
	# `(integer)`, `(boolean)`, `(double)` are written `(int)`, `(bool)`, `(float)`, and `( int )` is `(int)`
	castTypes: short

qualification:
	# `use \Acme\Shop\Order;` is written `use Acme\Shop\Order;`, an import being fully qualified anyway
	uselessBackslash: forbidden

imports:
	# `use function` below the imports of classes and `use const` last, each kind in the order written
	order: byKindOnly

# Every value is the construct written with its spacing; a comment names what else the same spacing covers.
spacing:
	# nothing inside the parentheses, not even around the `=`
	declare: 'declare(strict_types=1)'
	# no space before the parenthesis of a call, nor of a declaration, `function foo($a)`
	call: 'foo($a, $b)'
	# nothing inside any parentheses, of a call, a signature, a condition or an expression alike
	parentheses: '($a)'
	# after `elseif`, `while`, `for`, `foreach`, `switch`, `match` and `catch` too, and before the `{`
	controlKeyword: 'if ($a)'
	# around `catch`, `finally` and the `while` of `do` too, and before `as`, `insteadof` and the `use` of a closure,
	# each staying on the line of what precedes it
	connectingKeyword: '} else {'
	# the space after `function` of a closure, which the name of a function, `foo($x)`, does not have
	closure: 'function ($x)'
	# after `throw`, `yield`, `new`, `clone`, `include`, `print` and the other keywords followed by code too
	languageConstruct: 'return $x'
	# a line break after the comma is free
	comma: '$a, $b'
	# more spaces after a comma, aligning the columns of a table, collapse to one
	commaAlignment: none
	cast: '(int) $x'
	reference: '&$x'
	spread: '...$x'
	# the other unary operators too, `!$a`, `++$i`, `~$x`, and a variable variable, `$$a`
	unaryOperator: '-$x'
	# `! $x` may keep its space, as written
	unaryOperatorsWithSpace: [!]
	# around an assignment, `=>`, `instanceof` and the `=` of a default too; `.` has a key of its own
	binaryOperator: '$a + $b'
	concatenation: '$a . $b'
	# and around `?:` as a whole, `$a ?: $b`
	ternary: '$a ? $b : $c'
	# the head stays on one line, unless its interfaces are spread over lines
	classHead: 'class Foo extends Bar implements Baz'
	anonymousClass: 'new class ($a)'
	modifiers: 'final public static function'
	# nothing inside a type, one space before the name it declares, `): int` for a return type
	typeDeclaration: '?int $x'
	catchTypes: 'catch (A | B $e)'
	switchCase: 'case 1:'

multiline:
	operatorPosition:
		# a line broken at an operator other than `.` begins with the operator rather than the line before ending with it
		binary: lineStart
		# the boolean operators of a condition spanning lines stand all at the start of the lines
		condition: lineStart
	# a signature too long for its line gets every parameter on a line of its own
	signatureOverMaxLength: split
	# a constructor with promoted properties is spread only where its line is too long
	constructorWithPromotedProperties: asSignature
	# a signature, a call or a condition spread over lines has a line for every parameter, argument or part, the
	# parentheses standing on lines of their own:
	#     if (
	#         $a
	#         && $b
	#     ) {
	signature: perLine
	call: perLine
	condition: perLine

braces:
	# the `{` of a class, an interface, a trait, an enum and of a function whose parameters stand on one line goes
	# below the head
	class: nextLine
	function: nextLine
	# below parameters spread over lines, `) {` share a line of their own
	afterMultilineSignature: sameLine
	# the `{` of a closure, an anonymous class and a control structure stays on the line of its head
	closure: sameLine
	anonymousClass: sameLine
	controlStructure: sameLine
	# `if ($a) foo();` gets braces around its body
	controlStructureBody: required
	# `} else {`, `} catch (E $e) {`, `} while ($a);`
	continuingKeyword: sameLine
	# an empty body takes its lines as any other, `{` and `}` each on a line of its own
	emptyBody: ownLines
	# a closure written whole on one line, `function () { return 1; }`, is spread over lines
	singlelineClosure: forbidden

# One blank line ends each block of the header of a file, the opening tag, the namespace, the imports and each kind
# of them, and none follows the `{` of a class or precedes its `}`.
blankLines:
	afterOpeningTag: 1
	beforeNamespace: 1
	afterNamespace: 1
	afterImports: 1
	betweenImportKinds: 1
	beforeFirstMethod: 0
	afterLastMethod: 0
	beforeFirstMember: 0
	afterLastMember: 0
	# the trait uses one below another, and a blank line between them and the members that follow
	betweenTraitUses: 0
	afterTraitUses: 1

classes:
	# every property, method and constant says its visibility, `var` written `public`, and the modifiers stand in the
	# order `abstract` or `final`, visibility, `static`, `readonly`
	memberVisibility: required
	# a method of an interface says `public` too, though it is public anyway
	interfaceMethodVisibility: required
	# the trait uses before any other member
	memberOrder: [traitUse]
	# `public $a, $b;` is split into two declarations, and so is `use A, B;` inside a class
	onePerDeclaration: [property, traitUse]
	# `new Foo` is written `new Foo()`
	newParentheses: required

controlFlow:
	# `else if` is written `elseif`
	elseif: 'elseif'
	# `case 1;` is written `case 1:`
	switchCaseTerminator: ':'
	# a non-empty `case` falling through to the next one carries `// no break`, and is reported where it lacks it, only
	# the author knowing whether the fall-through is meant
	switchFallThrough: no break
```


`perCs`
=======

[PER Coding Style 3.1 |https://www.php-fig.org/per/coding-style/], nástupce PSR-12: k němu přidává čárky na konci víceřádkových seznamů, arrow funkce, prázdná těla `{}`, atributy, výčty, heredoc a property hooky.

```neon .[preset]
# PER Coding Style 3.1
#
# PSR-12 plus what PER Coding Style added (trailing commas, short closures, empty bodies as `{}`, attributes,
# enumerations, heredoc, property hooks); the specification defines the style and this preset adds nothing of its own.

use: psr12

indentation:
	# the body and the closing marker of a heredoc one level deeper than the line it begins on:
	#     $sql = <<<SQL
	#         SELECT 1
	#         SQL;
	heredoc: startPlusOne

naming:
	# `case Hearts;` of an enum, reported and never renamed as every other name
	enumCase: PascalCase

# Every value is the construct written with its spacing.
spacing:
	attribute: '#[Foo($a)]'
	arrowFunction: 'fn($x) => $x'
	# and the `;` stays on the line of what it ends
	beforeSemicolon: '$a;'
	# the bar of a multi-catch is spaced as in a union type, unlike in PSR-12
	catchTypes: 'catch (A|B $e)'
	namedArgument: 'foo(name: $x)'

multiline:
	operatorPosition:
		# a line broken at `.`, `?` or `:` begins with the operator, as at any other binary operator
		concatenation: lineStart
		ternary: lineStart
	# a chain, a ternary or an array spread over lines has every link, branch or item on a line of its own
	chain: perLine
	ternary: perLine
	array: perLine
	# a list spread over lines ends with a comma where its closing bracket stands on a line of its own, and a list on
	# one line never ends with one
	trailingComma:
		array: required
		argument: required
		parameter: required
		matchArm: required
		closureUse: required
		# the names of a group use and the items of `list()` spread over lines may end with a comma or not
		import: optional
		list: optional
	# every attribute group of a declaration on a line of its own above it, and of a parameter so where the
	# parameters are spread over lines
	attributes: ownLines
	parameterAttributes: ownLines

braces:
	# an empty body is `{}` on the line of the head, `class Foo {}`, `function foo(): void {}`, and an empty
	# anonymous class `new class {}`
	emptyBody: sameLine
	emptyAnonymousClass: sameLine

classes:
	# `const A = 1, B = 2;` is split into two declarations too
	onePerDeclaration: [constant, property, traitUse]
	# `public $a; public $b;` on one line is spread over two
	membersPerLine: 1
	# a doc comment stands above the attributes of its declaration, never between them and it
	phpdocAboveAttributes: required
	# `new class() {}` is written `new class {}`, `#[Foo()]` is written `#[Foo]`
	anonymousClassParentheses: forbidden
	attributeParentheses: forbidden

types:
	# `int|null` is written `?int`
	nullable: '?int'
	# `null|int|string` is written `int|string|null`
	nullPosition: last

literals:
	# a heredoc with nothing to interpolate is a nowdoc, `<<<'SQL'`
	heredocWithoutInterpolation: forbidden
	# `array(1, 2)` is written `[1, 2]`, `list($a, $b) =` is written `[$a, $b] =`
	longArraySyntax: forbidden
```


`nette`
=======

[Nette Coding Standard |https://doc.nette.org/cs/contributing/coding-standard]: PER Coding Style s tabulátory a rozvržením knihoven Nette, `declare(strict_types=1)` na řádku `<?php` a hygiena kódu, kterou knihovny Nette dodržují. Kromě `perCs` používá sady `cleanup`, `types` a `correctness` a pár jejich rozhodnutí vrací hodnotou `keep`: větev `else` za `return`, ladicí volání, třídu s `__toString()` bez `Stringable`, oba zápisy typu pole a nativní typy parametrů, vlastností a návratových hodnot. Projekt, který tytéž sady napíše vedle `nette`, je zpátky nedostane, protože každá sada leží jen jednou, pod `nette`; kdo je chce, napíše ta rozhodnutí sám.

```neon .[preset]
# Nette Coding Standard
#
# PER Coding Style with tabs and the layout of the Nette libraries, the hygiene of the code, and the choices the Nette
# libraries make: strict types declared on the line of the opening tag, how names are cased, in what order the members
# of a class stand, which functions and constructs are out, and what a doc comment of theirs holds. The layout departs
# from PER Coding Style in two blank lines between methods, none inside the braces of a body, one closing a branch or
# a case another one follows when its last statement stands apart, a tab that may align commas, the brace of
# a multi-line signature below a return type, promoted properties on lines of their own, an expression on the line of
# its return, and a chain, an array or a condition that may keep the shape it has.

use: [perCs, cleanup, types, correctness]

file:
	# `declare(strict_types=1);` in every file of PHP code, which is a risky fix: a call passing `'1'` to an `int`
	# parameter then throws
	strictTypes: required
	# `<?php declare(strict_types=1);`
	strictTypesPlacement: openingTagLine
	# a tab counting as four columns
	maxLineLength: 140

indentation:
	# a tab per level, where PER Coding Style has four spaces
	unit: tab
	# a link of a chain working on what the link before it returned may stand one level deeper, and the branches of
	# a ternary stand one level below a condition spread over lines:
	#     $class->addMethod('__construct')
	#         ->addPromotedParameter('container')
	#             ->setPrivate();
	ternaryBelowCondition: stepped
	chain: nested

naming:
	# the cases of the Nette libraries beside those of PSR-1, reported and never renamed as every other name: `fooBar()`
	# for a function, `$fooBar` for a property and a variable, and `DefaultTimeout` for a constant, where PSR-1 has
	# `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT`
	function: camelCase
	constant: PascalCase
	property: camelCase
	variable: camelCase
	# `FooInterface`, `FooTrait`, `AbstractFoo` and a plain class named `FooError` are reported
	classKindInName: forbidden

builtin:
	# `__dir__` is written `__DIR__`
	magicConstants: uppercase
	# a class and a function of PHP are written as PHP declares them, `datetime` as `DateTime`, `StrLen()` as `strlen()`
	classes: declared
	functions: declared

qualification:
	# `new \Acme\Shop\Order` is written `new Order` below `use Acme\Shop\Order;`
	classOfAnotherNamespace: imported
	# `Foo::bar()` and `new Foo` inside `Foo` are written `self::bar()` and `new self`
	currentClass: self

imports:
	# classes, then functions, then constants, each kind in alphabetical order
	order: byKind
	# a `use` for every class, and the functions and the constants each in one `use`:
	#     use Nette\Utils\Arrays;
	#     use Nette\Utils\Strings;
	#     use function count, is_array;
	classes: separate
	functions: combined
	constants: combined

# Every value is the construct written with its spacing.
spacing:
	# tabs after a comma aligning the columns of a table may stay
	commaAlignment: tabs
	# a `;` followed by more code on its line
	semicolon: 'for ($i = 0; $i < 5; $i++)'
	# `! $x` is written `!$x`, no unary operator keeping a space
	unaryOperatorsWithSpace: []
	# more spaces around `?` and `:` collapse to one
	ternaryAlignment: none
	doubleColon: 'Foo::bar()'
	objectOperator: '$a->b()'
	offsetBrackets: '$a[0]'
	arrayBrackets: '[1, 2]'
	# a space after the marker of `//`, `#` and `/*` and before `*/`, a ruler such as `////` excepted
	comment: '// text'
	# at least one space between the code and a comment following it on its line
	commentAfterCode: '$a; // text'

multiline:
	# an expression spanning lines begins on the line of `return`, `throw`, `yield`, `print` or `echo`, `return [` rather
	# than `return` above a lone `[`
	expressionBelowReturn: forbidden
	# the `;` of a statement spanning lines closes its last line rather than standing alone below it
	semicolonOnOwnLine: forbidden
	# a constructor with promoted properties has every parameter on a line of its own, however short
	constructorWithPromotedProperties: split
	# the first link of a chain may share the line of the object, `$form->addText('name')` above `->setRequired()`
	chainFirstLinks: startLine
	# a broken condition may begin on the line of its parenthesis, `if ($a` above `&& $b`, or below it; one in neither
	# shape is written in the first
	condition: [perLine, compact]
	# several items may share a line, an array wider than 130 characters is spread
	array: asWritten
	arrayOverWidth: 130
	trailingComma:
		matchArm: keep
		closureUse: keep

braces:
	# below a signature spread over lines, the `{` stands on a line of its own where a return type ends it:
	#     public function foo(
	#         int $a,
	#     ): Foo
	#     {
	afterMultilineSignature: nextLineAfterReturnType
	# an empty body takes its lines as any other, where PER Coding Style writes `{}`
	emptyBody: ownLines
	emptyAnonymousClass: keep
	singlelineClosure: keep
	# `if (...): ... endif;` and the other colon forms are written with braces
	alternativeSyntax: forbidden

# A count of blank lines, or a range `[1, 2]` within which the author chooses.
blankLines:
	afterOpeningTag: keep
	# the imports of all kinds form one block
	betweenImportKinds: 0
	# two blank lines above the class or the function the header of a file leads to, one or two around a declaration
	# among statements
	beforeDeclaration: 2
	betweenDeclarations: [1, 2]
	# two blank lines between methods, one between the methods of an interface, which have no body
	betweenMethods: 2
	betweenInterfaceMethods: 1
	# properties, constants and enum cases may stand one below another or a blank line apart, while one with a doc
	# comment or an attribute takes a blank line above it and none below it
	betweenMembers: [0, 1]
	beforeDocumentedMember: 1
	afterPhpdoc: 0
	# no blank line after the `{` of a block, at most one before its `}`
	afterBlockOpeningBrace: 0
	beforeBlockClosingBrace: [0, 1]
	# a branch or a case another one follows ends with a blank line where its last statement stands apart, so that it
	# does not read as the start of the next one:
	#     if ($a) {
	#         foo();
	#
	#         return 1;
	#
	#     } else {
	betweenBranches: lastStatementSetApart
	betweenCases: lastStatementSetApart

classes:
	# a method of an interface is public whatever it says, so it says nothing
	interfaceMethodVisibility: forbidden
	# the trait uses, then the constants, then the properties, each by visibility; the methods follow in the order written
	memberOrder: [traitUse, constant, publicConstant, protectedConstant, privateConstant, publicProperty, protectedProperty, privateProperty]
	# `const A = 1, B = 2;` may stay, unlike in PER Coding Style
	onePerDeclaration: [property, traitUse]
	# `new Foo()` is written `new Foo`, the parentheses that `new Foo()->bar()` needs staying
	newParentheses: forbidden

types:
	# `int $x = null` is written `?int $x = null`
	defaultNull: '?int $x = null'
	# `/** @var Foo $x */` above an assignment is written as `assert($x instanceof Foo)` below it, a risky fix, the
	# assertion failing where the annotation was wrong
	inlineVarAnnotation: forbidden
	# a type is written where it says something, a closure needs no `void` and an array no annotation of its items
	parameter: keep
	property: keep
	return: keep

functions:
	# a function declared inside a function, a method or a closure, which exists only once that runs, is reported
	innerFunctions: forbidden
	# `function ($x) { return $x * 2; }` is written `fn($x) => $x * 2`, a closure holding another one too
	closureReturningOneExpression: forbidden
	closureReturningOneExpressionNested: forbidden

calls:
	# a debugging call may stay as it is
	debugOutput: keep
	# `is_null($x)` is written `$x === null`
	is_null: forbidden
	# `settype($x, 'int')` is written `$x = (int) $x`
	settype: forbidden
	# `intval($x)` is written `(int) $x`
	conversionFunctions: forbidden
	# `dirname(__FILE__)` is written `__DIR__`
	dirnameOfFile: forbidden

controlFlow:
	# a non-empty `case` falling through to the next one carries `// break omitted`, and is reported where it lacks it
	switchFallThrough: break omitted
	# an else after a return may stay
	elseAfterExit: keep
	# `global $config;` is reported
	globalStatement: forbidden

expressions:
	# `==` and `!=` are written `===` and `!==`, a risky fix where a loose comparison of different types answers
	# otherwise; `// intentionally ==` keeps one, see `suppressionComments`
	comparison: strict
	# `<>` is written `!=`
	notEquals: '!='
	# `1 === $a` is written `$a === 1`
	yoda: forbidden
	# `and` and `or` are written `&&` and `||` where the meaning stays, `xor` staying
	wordLogicalOperators: forbidden
	# `$a && $b || $c` is written `($a && $b) || $c`, and `$a & $b == 1` is written `$a & ($b == 1)`, as PHP reads it
	explicitPrecedence: required
	# `$i += 1` is written `$i++`
	incrementByAssignment: forbidden
	# `$a = $a + $b` is written `$a += $b`
	assignmentRepeatingTarget: forbidden
	# `!!$a` is written `(bool) $a`
	doubleNegation: forbidden
	# `$a ? $a : $b` is written `$a ?: $b`
	ternaryReturningItsCondition: forbidden
	# `isset($a) ? $a : $b` is written `$a ?? $b`
	ternaryTestingNull: forbidden
	# `get_class()` and `__CLASS__` are written `self::class`, `get_called_class()` is written `static::class`
	getClassCalls: forbidden
	# `get_class($o)` is written `$o::class`
	getClassOnObjects: forbidden
	# `isset($a) && isset($b)` is written `isset($a, $b)`
	separateIssets: forbidden
	# `unset($a); unset($b);` is written `unset($a, $b);`
	consecutiveUnsets: forbidden
	# the backtick operator is written `shell_exec()`
	backticks: forbidden

literals:
	# `"text"` is written `'text'`, double quotes staying where they interpolate or escape
	quotes: single
	# in double quotes and a heredoc, `"\d+"` is written `"\\d+"`, every backslash that escapes nothing doubled
	backslashes: escaped
	# `1000000` is written `1_000_000`, a number of up to six digits staying as it is
	digitGroupsFrom: 7
	# a fraction of twenty digits and more is grouped too, `0.000_001`
	fractionDigitGroupsFrom: 20

comments:
	# `# text` is written `// text`
	singleLine: '//'

phpdoc:
	# `@Param`, `@inheritdoc` are written `@param`, `@inheritDoc`
	annotations: canonicalCase
	# every `*` of a doc comment right below the first `*` of its `/**`
	stars: aligned
	# no blank line opening or closing a doc comment, and at most one in a row inside it
	blankLinesAtEdges: forbidden
	# a plain comment above a property, `// the count` or `/* the count */`, is reported where a doc comment belongs
	propertyComment: phpdoc
	# a doc comment of a property with one line of content takes one line, `/** @var int */`
	propertyPhpdocOfOneLine: singleline
	# a promoted property is annotated by a `@var` of its own, not by a `@param` of the constructor
	promotedPropertyAnnotation: '@var'
	# what the repository and the language say better, removed with their lines
	forbiddenAnnotations: [@access, @author, @copyright, @created, @license, @package, @since, @subpackage, @todo, @version]
	# the descriptions that say nothing, `Constructor.`, `Created by John.`, `Name getter.`, removed
	forbiddenLines: ['~^(?:(?!private|protected|static)\S+ )?(?:con|de)structor\.\z~i', ~^Created by \S+\.\z~i, '~^\S+ [gs]etter\.\z~i']
	types:
		# both notations of an array type stay as they are
		array: keep
		# `null|int` is written `int|null` in a doc comment as in a declaration
		nullPosition: last

upgrading:
	php:
		# `"${name}"` is written `"{$name}"`, PHP 8.2 having deprecated the former
		dollarBraceInterpolation: forbidden
	syntax:
		# `017` is written `0o17`
		octalPrefix: adopted
	classes:
		# a class with `__toString()` is `Stringable` without saying so
		Stringable: keep

# A comment that explains an exception keeps the decision quiet on its line: `// intentionally ==` a loose comparison,
# and `// @ <why>` an `@` operator.
suppressionComments:
	'~\bintentionally\s+[!=]=~': expressions.comparison
	'~^//\s*@\s+\S~': correctness.errorSuppression
```


`symfony`
=========

Symfony Coding Standards tak, jak je definuje sada `@Symfony` PHP CS Fixeru, zatím bez většiny jejích pravidel pro phpDoc.

```neon .[preset]
# Symfony Coding Standards as the `@Symfony` rule set defines them, without most of its phpDoc rules
#
# The Symfony Coding Standards as the @Symfony rule set of PHP CS Fixer defines them, without most of its rules about
# phpDoc, of which it takes only an empty doc comment, the trimming and the canonical types: PER Coding Style, which the
# set builds on, with the casing, the imports, the blank lines and the whitespace Symfony adds, and without the rules
# that would break a construct over lines, which Symfony leaves to the author.

use: perCs

file:
	maxLineLength: none

indentation:
	binaryOperator: keep
	chain: keep
	# heredoc_indentation belongs to another set
	heredoc: keep

builtin:
	magicConstants: uppercase
	classes: declared
	functions: declared

qualification:
	# global_namespace_import imports nothing: a class is written fully qualified, a function and a constant too where
	# they are qualified, and a bare one stays bare
	globalClass: fullyQualified
	globalFunction:
		normally: [fullyQualified, bare]
		optimizedByCompiler: same
	globalConstant:
		normally: [fullyQualified, bare]
		computedByCompiler: same

imports:
	order: byKind
	classes: separate
	functions: separate
	constants: separate
	groupUse: forbidden
	unused: forbidden

spacing:
	arrowFunction: 'fn ($x) => $x'
	commaAlignment: any
	semicolon: 'for ($i = 0; $i < 5; $i++)'
	unaryOperatorsWithSpace: []
	binaryOperatorAlignment: none
	concatenation: '$a.$b'
	objectOperator: '$a->b()'
	offsetBrackets: '$a[0]'
	arrayBrackets: '[1, 2]'
	anonymousClass: 'new class($a)'
	comment: '// text'
	commentAfterCode: '$a; // text'

multiline:
	operatorPosition:
		# operator_linebreak moves only a boolean operator, which no option here tells from the others
		binary: keep
		concatenation: keep
		ternary: keep
		condition: keep
	signatureOverMaxLength: keep
	signature: keep
	call: keep
	# no fixer of the set breaks a chain, a condition, a ternary or an array
	chain: keep
	condition: keep
	ternary: keep
	array: keep
	trailingComma:
		argument: optional
		closureUse: keep
	parameterAttributes: keep

braces:
	emptyBody: ownLines
	emptyAnonymousClass: keep
	singlelineClosure: keep
	bareStatementGroup: forbidden
	alternativeSyntax: forbidden

blankLines:
	betweenDeclarations: [0, 1]
	betweenMethods: 1
	betweenInterfaceMethods: 1
	betweenTraitUses: keep
	afterTraitUses: keep
	afterPhpdoc: 0
	beforeStatement: {return: [1, null]}

classes:
	untypedPropertyNullInitialization: forbidden

types:
	defaultNull: '?int $x = null'

functions:
	trailingBareReturn: forbidden

controlFlow:
	elseAfterExit: forbidden

expressions:
	notEquals: '!='
	incrementByAssignment: forbidden
	doubleNegation: forbidden
	parenthesesAfterConstruct: forbidden
	backticks: forbidden

literals:
	quotes: single
	# heredoc_to_nowdoc belongs to another set
	heredocWithoutInterpolation: keep

comments:
	singleLine: '//'
	empty: forbidden

phpdoc:
	blankLinesAtEdges: forbidden
	empty: forbidden
	types:
		builtin: canonical
		nullPosition: last

correctness:
	continueInSwitch: forbidden

upgrading:
	php:
		dollarBraceInterpolation: forbidden
```


Sady
====

Sada nerozhoduje nic o vzhledu kódu, a proto se se standardem nikdy nepere. Pokládá se vedle něj (`use: [nette, modernizations]`) a hlavně roste: rozhodnutí, které DressCode v nové verzi získá, přibude do své sady, a projekt, který ji rozšiřuje, ho dostane bez změny konfigurace.


`modernizations`
================

Konstrukce novějšího PHP tam, kde totéž říká starší zápis, každá až od verze, kterou cíl projektu dovolí, a novější zápis, který nabízejí soubory dat nainstalovaných balíčků.

```neon .[preset]
# Modernizations
#
# The construct a newer PHP has, written where an older one says the same, each where the target version of the
# project has it, and the newer form the upgrading files of the installed packages offer. It decides nothing about the
# layout, so it goes with any standard.

functions:
	closureReturningOneExpression: forbidden
	closureReturningOneExpressionNested: forbidden

controlFlow:
	ifReturningOneOfTwoValues: forbidden

expressions:
	getClassCalls: forbidden
	assignmentRepeatingTarget: forbidden
	ternaryTestingNull: forbidden
	ternaryReturningItsCondition: forbidden
	separateIssets: forbidden
	consecutiveUnsets: forbidden

literals:
	longArraySyntax: forbidden

upgrading:
	libraries:
		modernizations: adopted
	php:
		# soft-deprecated, with the newer `__serialize()` and `__unserialize()` to write instead
		sleepAndWakeup: forbidden
	syntax:
		spreadMerge: adopted
		dynamicClassConstant: adopted
		match: adopted
		throwExpression: adopted
		catchWithoutVariable: adopted
		cloneWith: adopted
		nullsafe: adopted
		pipe: adopted
		newWithoutParentheses: adopted
		firstClassCallables: adopted
		octalPrefix: adopted
	functions:
		array_is_list: adopted
		arraySearchFunctions: adopted
		arrayFirstLast: adopted
		clamp: adopted
		get_debug_type: adopted
		json_validate: adopted
		substringFunctions: adopted
		RoundingMode: adopted
	classes:
		promotedProperties: adopted
		newInInitializer: adopted
	phpdoc:
		Deprecated: adopted
```


`deprecations`
==============

Co novější PHP zavrhlo nebo zrušilo, opravené tam, kde náhrada existuje, a ohlášené tam, kde ne, a co soubory dat nainstalovaných balíčků uvádějí jako zavržené.

```neon .[preset]
# Deprecations
#
# What a newer PHP deprecated or removed, fixed where a replacement exists and reported where none does, and what the
# upgrading files of the installed packages list as retired. A deprecation is reported whatever the target, the code
# meeting it wherever it runs on the version that made it.

builtin:
	castTypes: short

classes:
	overridingSignature: asAncestor
	overridingParameterNames: asAncestor

types:
	defaultNull: nullable

controlFlow:
	switchCaseTerminator: colon

expressions:
	backticks: forbidden

literals:
	nullArrayKey: forbidden

correctness:
	finalParent: forbidden
	unimplementedAbstractMethods: forbidden
	__serialize: required

upgrading:
	libraries:
		deprecations: forbidden
		deprecatedClasses: replaced
		deprecatedMembers: replaced
	php:
		guide: forbidden
		constructorReturnValue: forbidden
		sleepAndWakeup: forbidden
		returnInFinally: forbidden
		csvDefaultEscape: forbidden
		dollarBraceInterpolation: forbidden
		reservedNames: forbidden
	syntax:
		firstClassCallables: adopted
```


`cleanup`
=========

Kód, který je tam pro nic: co opakuje, co jazyk už říká, co se nikdy nevykoná, alias funkce, komentář, který nic neříká.

```neon .[preset]
# Cleanup
#
# Code that is there for nothing: what repeats what the language already says, what can never run, an alias of a
# function, a comment or a doc comment that says nothing. It decides nothing about the layout, so it goes with any
# standard.

file:
	emptyStatements: forbidden

qualification:
	uselessBackslash: forbidden
	inFileWithoutNamespace: bare

imports:
	unused: forbidden
	aliasEqualToName: forbidden
	ofCurrentNamespace: forbidden

braces:
	bareStatementGroup: forbidden

classes:
	impliedModifiers: forbidden
	untypedPropertyNullInitialization: forbidden
	methodOnlyCallingParent: forbidden
	ReturnTypeWillChange: forbidden

functions:
	trailingBareReturn: forbidden
	unreachableParameterDefault: forbidden

calls:
	debugOutput: commentedOut
	aliasFunctions: [internal, imap, pg]
	call_user_func: forbidden
	explicitInvokeCalls: forbidden
	uselessArguments: forbidden

controlFlow:
	ifReturningBoolean: forbidden
	elseAfterExit: forbidden

expressions:
	parenthesesAfterConstruct: forbidden
	ternaryOfTrueAndFalse: forbidden

literals:
	classNameInString: forbidden
	manualEmptyTest: forbidden
	concatenatedLiterals: joined

comments:
	empty: forbidden

phpdoc:
	empty: forbidden
	constantVar: forbidden
	repeatingNativeTypes: forbidden
	inheritdocOnly: forbidden

upgrading:
	php:
		# a call doing nothing on the target, `curl_close()` among them, goes with the rest of the guide
		guide: forbidden
	syntax:
		catchWithoutVariable: adopted
		newWithoutParentheses: adopted
```


`correctness`
=============

To, co je nejspíš chyba, ať je styl jakýkoli.

```neon .[preset]
# Correctness
#
# What is most likely a mistake whatever the style: a call comparing loosely where it should not, `$this` where no
# object is, a `catch` nothing reaches, a doc comment contradicting itself, invisible characters in the code.

phpdoc:
	consistency:
		paramOfUnknownParameter: forbidden
		duplicateReturn: forbidden
		emptyAnnotation: forbidden
		duplicateVar: forbidden

correctness:
	__debugInfo: array
	thisOutsideObject: forbidden
	__set_state: static
	continueInSwitch: forbidden
	unreachableCatch: forbidden
	exceptionWhereThrowableBelongs: forbidden
	errorSuppression: forbidden
	invisibleCharacters: forbidden
	strictCalls: required
	trailingWhitespaceInStrings: forbidden
	consecutivePhpdocs: forbidden
	repeatedAssignment: forbidden
```


`types`
=======

Typy zapsané tam, kde je čte PHP.

```neon .[preset]
# Types
#
# Types written where PHP reads them: a native type on every parameter, property and return that has one, the
# shortest notation of a type, `never` on a function that only throws, `Stringable` on a class with `__toString()`.

types:
	parameter: required
	property: required
	return: required
	nullable: questionMark
	nullPosition: last

phpdoc:
	types:
		builtin: canonical
		array: generic

upgrading:
	classes:
		Stringable: adopted
		neverReturnType: adopted
```


`optimizedCalls`
================

Volání ve tvaru, který PHP optimalizuje už při překladu, viz [Optimalizace funkcí a konstant |optimizations].

```neon .[preset]
# Optimized calls
#
# The arguments of a call the compiler optimizes written so that it still can.

qualification:
	globalFunction:
		# every form passes, so no name is rewritten; what the compiler already optimizes keeps its arguments positional
		optimizedByCompiler: [imported, fullyQualified, bare]
```
